<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Chem sees '97 sales at 4.1 trln won.</title>
<headline>LG Chem sees '97 sales at 4.1 trln won.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's LG Chemical Ltd, a unit of LG Group, said on Tuesday it expected its sales to reach 4.1 trillion won this year against 3.5 trillion in 1996.  </p>
<p>A company spokesman said LG Chemical expected a sharp rise in net profit this year from last year's 3.31 billion won.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect a strong performance in both sales and net profit due to an improvement in the petrochemical business,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>A rise in petrochemical product prices and a fall in prices of naphtha, the feed stock for petrochemicals, were expected to contribute to healthy growth, he said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
